---
description: Code conventions mirrored from the eZsign production front-end
globs: "**/*.vue,**/*.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Block order in `.vue`: `<template>`, `<script setup lang="ts">`, `<style scoped>`.
- 3-space indentation.
- English identifiers and comments. UI text in French through `$gettext('…')` in templates and `gettext('…')` in scripts (from `@ez`). Interpolation: `$gettext('Rappel envoyé à %{name}.', { name })`.
- Local refs/state named `the*` (`theData`, `theFolder`, `theTargets`). UI state in `theUI` (`{ $isLoading, $dialogs: { … } }`).
- Business logic stays in the mock objects' methods (`folder.isStateClosed()`, `signer.canBeReminded()`), not re-implemented in templates.
- Icons: `:icon="ez.icons.send"`.
- Class strings may use `block-name || utilities` to separate a BEM name from utilities.
- French copy: no space before a colon.
- Keep it readable over clever: the team lead prefers simple code.
